  "notes": "{漏電|ろうでん} refers to electrical current leaking through unintended paths, a serious safety hazard.\n\nWRITING:\n- {漏|ろう} (leak)\n- {電|でん} (electricity)\n\nSAFETY CONCERN:\n- Can cause electrical fires\n- Can lead to electric shock\n- Often caused by aged or damaged insulation\n\nCOMPOUNDS:\n- {漏電|ろうでん}{遮断|しゃだん}{器|き} (earth leakage circuit breaker / ELCB)\n- {漏電|ろうでん}{火災|かさい} (fire caused by electrical leak)\n- {漏電|ろうでん}{検査|けんさ} (electrical leak inspection)\n\nUSAGE:\n- {漏電|ろうでん}する (to have an electrical leak - suru verb)\n- {漏電|ろうでん}している (there is an electrical leak)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {感電|かんでん} (electric shock)\n- {配線|はいせん} (wiring)\n- ブレーカー (circuit breaker)",
